    <string name="pref_aacp">Hardware control channel</string>
    <string name="pref_aacp_desc">Keeps a separate control link (L2CAP) to the AirPods so noise control, ear detection, conversation awareness and other settings can be read and changed. If you only need the battery display, turn this off to save the power and connection overhead of that always-on link. The items on the "AirPods settings" screen will then be hidden.</string>
    <string name="pref_aacp_battery">Read battery over the control channel</string>
    <string name="pref_aacp_battery_desc">The default battery display reads the Bluetooth advertisement (beacon) the AirPods broadcast nearby. That beacon carries no device identifier and its MAC address keeps rotating, so if someone next to you is also using AirPods there is no way to be completely sure which reading is yours.\n\nWith this on, whenever the "Hardware control channel" above is connected the battery is requested directly over that channel. The channel is established only with the exact AirPods paired to this phone, so readings can never be mixed up, and left/right/case levels come through even while Bluetooth scanning is off.\n\nOn devices where the control channel does not connect (unsupported model, failed link) it automatically falls back to the beacon method. Requires the "Hardware control channel" above to be on.</string>
